course: dictionary
lesson: 14207
title: Mudslide
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A mudslide is a large amount of wet mud sliding quickly down a hill or mountain. You can work out its meaning from the words around it. «After three days of heavy rain, a mudslide blocked the road up the mountain.» Heavy rain and a blocked road tell you the mud came down fast and stopped the traffic.
explain: The clues can also tell you where a mudslide happens. «The steep hill had lost its trees, so the soil was loose and a mudslide started.» Steep slopes, missing trees and loose soil are the clues that help a mudslide happen.
explain: Sometimes the word has a fun meaning too. «At the adventure park, we rode the mudslide and came out covered in mud.» Here a mudslide is a slippery slide in mud, not a danger. Always swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A mudslide is a large amount of wet mud sliding quickly down a hill or mountain.
fact: Mudslides often happen after heavy rain.
fact: Rain can loosen soil on steep slopes, so the mud slides down.
fact: Trees hold soil in place, so cutting them down makes a mudslide more likely.
fact: Mudslides can bury roads and houses, so people are warned to leave when heavy rain is coming. Informally, a mudslide is also a fun slippery slide in mud.
exercise: «After three days of heavy rain, a mudslide blocked the road.» What blocked the road? | *A mudslide | A wooden bridge | A tall tree | A herd of sheep
exercise: What usually makes a mudslide more likely on a steep hill? | *Heavy rain | A calm, quiet morning | Snow falling on a beach | A sunny, dry week
exercise: «The steep hill had lost its trees, so the soil was loose and a mudslide started.» Find and copy the word that tells you the hill was not flat. | soil | hill | *steep | trees
test: «The warning said people must leave, because a mudslide could bury their houses.» What could a mudslide do to houses? | Give them a new roof | Paint them bright colours | *Bury them | Make them float away like boats
test: Ella says a mudslide is always a bad thing. Which statement is true? | A mudslide only happens on flat ground | A mudslide is a kind of sweet cake | A mudslide is always made of sand | *A mudslide can also be a fun slippery slide in mud
exam: Which sentence uses mudslide in its first meaning? | Our dog had a mudslide bath | I ate a mudslide cake at the party | The sun made the mudslide warm and bright | *A mudslide covered the road after the storm
